```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
Both scripts return the same customer‐month pair (customer 148, 2005‑07) and the same numeric change (77.83).  
However, 2result.sql keeps the true signed month‑over‑month difference until the final projection (it applies ABS only for ordering), so the underlying calculation is correct whether the largest change is an increase or a decrease. 1result.sql converts the difference to an absolute value immediately, discarding sign information; therefore 2result.sql is the more accurate and generally safer choice.